{"author":{"id":"836d943203cf5a4f01ab5d4b4780de84949c43734f2256a167cc5931ae5d8c66"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794180688,"nonce":"xDu+I+P1A0eNiMi9yS6rdUVSXmE=","title":"L1 — Issue list rows render blank or collapsed","message":"## Symptom\nOn the Issues page the rows are invisible (\"3 of 244 issues\" with an empty list). After picking `All` they show as tall, narrow, empty boxes next to their reopen buttons. They should be full-width cards with the title, meta and state.\n\n## Repro\n1. `cargo run` with at least one repo that has git-bug issues\n2. Open Issues: the list area is empty although the header counts rows\n3. Click `All`: each row is a ~100px-wide empty card next to its toggle button\n\n## Cause\n`src/ui/screen.rs:767` — the list `column![]` has no explicit width. Every row is a `lazy(...)` (`screen.rs:909`), and `Lazy::size_hint` always returns `Shrink` (`iced_widget-0.14.2/src/lazy.rs:157`). `Column::push` widens the column using each child's `size_hint` (`iced_widget-0.14.2/src/column.rs:145`), so the column stays `Shrink`. The `width(Fill)` card inside each row (`screen.rs:1000`) then gets almost no width and its text wraps to nothing.\n\n## Files\n- `src/ui/screen.rs:767` — list column\n- `src/ui/screen.rs:1022` — row container in `issue_card`\n\n## Approach\n- Split the list-building part of `issues()` (`screen.rs:743`) into `fn issue_list(app) -\u003e Element` and give the column `.width(Fill)`\n- Give the row container in `issue_card` `.width(Fill)` too, so a row never depends on its parent's width\n- Look for any other column whose children are only `lazy` and fix it the same way\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Repro step 2 shows the filtered rows as full-width cards; step 3 shows all rows readable\n- Unit test: `issue_list(\u0026app).as_widget().size().width == Length::Fill` for a booted app with issues (use the `src/testutil.rs` helpers)\n- Gates pass","files":null}]}